Module 2: UPLIFT HEALTH — Health & Wellness
Tagline: "Whole health, whole community. Care that sees you."

Problem Statement
Healthcare disparities for Black Americans are among the most devastating manifestations of systemic racism. Black women face a maternal mortality rate of 44.8 deaths per 100,000 live births — over three times the rate for white women (14.2). These disparities could worsen, with projections suggesting the rate could nearly double to 94 per 100,000 by 2040 without intervention. Mental health stigma in Black communities creates a treatment gap where conditions go unaddressed. Food deserts disproportionately affect Black neighborhoods — over 19 million Americans live in food deserts, with Black communities overrepresented. Chronic diseases including hypertension, diabetes, and heart disease affect Black Americans at significantly higher rates, yet access to culturally competent care remains limited.

Core Features
Feature	Description
Telehealth Connector	Connects users with culturally competent healthcare providers for virtual visits. Filters providers by specialty, language, cultural competency rating, insurance acceptance, and sliding-scale availability. Integrated video, chat, and phone visit options.
Mental Health Screening & Referral	Validated screening tools (PHQ-9 for depression, GAD-7 for anxiety) with culturally adapted language. Anonymous completion option. Automated referral engine connecting users to therapists, counselors, and support groups with cultural competency.
Community Health Worker (CHW) Coordination	Case management tool for CHWs to track patient outreach, social determinants of health assessments, care plan progress, and referral follow-up. Supports field data collection and offline access.
Food Access Mapper	Interactive map showing food banks, community gardens, farmers' markets accepting SNAP/EBT, free meal programs, and grocery delivery services. Real-time availability updates. SNAP/WIC benefit eligibility checker and enrollment assistance.
Maternal Health Tracker	Pregnancy and postpartum health tracking with milestone reminders, symptom logging, risk factor monitoring, and direct connection to maternal care providers. Culturally informed content addressing birth plan creation, doula matching, and postpartum mental health.
Chronic Disease Management Dashboard	Personal health dashboard for managing hypertension, diabetes, asthma, and heart disease. Medication reminders, vitals tracking, provider communication, and educational content on disease management.
Wellness Content Library	Curated library of culturally relevant health and wellness content: articles, videos, podcasts, and guided exercises covering nutrition, fitness, mental health, stress management, and preventive care.
Provider Directory with Cultural Competency Ratings	Searchable directory where providers are rated on cultural competency by community members. Includes verified credentials, accepted insurance, specialties, languages, and appointment availability.
User Stories
As a pregnant Black woman in a rural area, I want to connect with a culturally competent OB-GYN via telehealth so that I receive quality prenatal care without a 90-minute drive to the nearest hospital.
As a young man experiencing anxiety, I want to complete a confidential mental health screening on my phone so that I can understand my symptoms and find a therapist who understands my experience without judgment.
As a community health worker, I want to track my patient caseload and referral outcomes in one tool so that I can ensure continuity of care and report impact to my organization.
As a single father in a food desert, I want to find SNAP-accepting grocery options and community meal programs near me so that my children have consistent access to nutritious food.
