Module 3: UPLIFT WEALTH — Financial Empowerment
Tagline: "Build wealth. Break cycles. Own your future."

Problem Statement
The racial wealth gap is not narrowing — it is growing. From 2019 to 2022, the mean gap in net worth between Black and white households grew from $841,900 to $1.15 million, a 38% increase that far outpaced inflation. The median wealth of Black households ($24,520) is roughly one-tenth the median wealth of white households ($250,400). Nearly one in four Black households have zero or negative net worth. Black Americans carry higher student loan debt, face higher rates of predatory lending, and are disproportionately unbanked or underbanked. Credit deserts — areas with limited access to fair credit — overlap heavily with Black neighborhoods. Without targeted financial empowerment tools, the wealth gap will continue to compound across generations.

Core Features
Feature	Description
Financial Literacy Curriculum	Gamified, culturally relevant financial education covering budgeting, saving, investing, credit, debt management, insurance, and retirement planning. Badges, streaks, and community leaderboards drive engagement. Content co-created with Black financial educators.
Budgeting & Savings Goal Tracker	Linked-account budgeting tool (via Plaid) with automated categorization, spending insights, and savings goal visualization. Supports emergency fund building, debt paydown tracking, and custom savings goals (e.g., "first home," "business launch").
Credit Score Education & Monitoring Referral	Educational modules on how credit works, how to build/repair credit, and common predatory practices to avoid. Referrals to free credit monitoring services. Simulated credit score impact calculator ("What happens if I pay this off?").
Predatory Lending Alert System	AI-powered tool that analyzes loan terms and flags predatory characteristics (excessive APR, balloon payments, prepayment penalties). Connects users to CDFI alternatives and legal aid if they've been targeted.
CDFI & Community Bank Connector	Directory of Community Development Financial Institutions and Black-owned banks/credit unions. Filters by product type (personal loan, small business loan, mortgage), geography, and eligibility. Application referral workflow.
Homeownership Readiness Assessment	Guided assessment evaluating credit, savings, debt-to-income ratio, and local market conditions. Generates personalized homeownership plan with milestones, timelines, and resource connections (HUD counselors, down payment assistance programs).
Tax Preparation Assistance Locator	Map of free/low-cost tax preparation services (VITA sites, AARP Tax-Aide), IRS Free File tools, and EITC eligibility checker. Seasonal reminders and document preparation checklists.
Emergency Fund & Mutual Aid Tools	Community-based mutual aid fund management. Users can contribute to and request from neighborhood emergency funds. Transparent tracking, community-set eligibility criteria, and automated disbursement workflows.
User Stories
As a young professional with student loan debt, I want to understand my full financial picture and create a debt paydown plan so that I can become debt-free and start building wealth within 5 years.
As a first-time homebuyer, I want to assess my homeownership readiness and find down payment assistance programs so that I can create a realistic path to owning a home.
As a community member targeted by a payday lender, I want to have loan terms analyzed for predatory characteristics and be connected to fair alternatives so that I avoid a debt trap.
As a parent, I want to complete gamified financial literacy modules with my teenager so that they build financial habits I never had the chance to learn.
