Module 5: UPLIFT JUSTICE — Legal Aid & Criminal Justice
Tagline: "Know your rights. Reclaim your future. Justice is not optional."

Problem Statement
The United States incarcerates nearly two million people, with Black Americans incarcerated at six times the rate of white Americans. One in three Black boys born today can expect to be incarcerated during their lifetime, compared to 1 in 17 white boys. About 74% of Black adults believe the prison system was designed to hold Black people back. The consequences extend far beyond prison walls: imprisonment leads to declining employment prospects, lower earnings, food insecurity, housing instability, and devastating impacts on children and families. Record expungement — which could restore opportunities for millions — remains bureaucratically complex and inaccessible to most who qualify. Affordable legal aid is scarce, with 86% of civil legal problems reported by low-income Americans receiving inadequate or no legal help.

Core Features
Feature	Description
Know-Your-Rights Resource Library	Interactive, scenario-based learning modules: "What to do during a traffic stop," "Your rights during a protest," "Tenant rights when facing eviction," etc. Video, text, and audio formats. State-specific legal information. Available offline.
Legal Aid Directory & Intake	Searchable directory of pro bono attorneys, legal aid organizations, law school clinics, and public defenders. Online intake form that pre-qualifies users for services and routes them to appropriate providers by practice area and geography.
Record Expungement Eligibility Checker	State-by-state eligibility assessment based on charge type, conviction date, sentence completion, and subsequent record. Guides eligible users through document preparation and filing. NLP-powered analysis of court records to identify qualifying offenses.
Bail Fund Connector	Directory of community bail funds by jurisdiction. Request submission workflow for families needing bail assistance. Donation portal for community members supporting bail reform. Transparent fund tracking.
Police Accountability & Incident Reporting	Secure, encrypted incident reporting tool for documenting interactions with law enforcement. Timestamp, location, officer identification, narrative, and media upload. Reports can be shared with legal advocates, oversight bodies, or kept private. Community-level incident mapping (anonymized).
Reentry Support Resource Hub	Comprehensive resource directory for formerly incarcerated individuals: housing, employment, counseling, substance abuse treatment, ID restoration, voter rights restoration, and family reunification services. Personalized reentry plan builder.
Court Date Tracker & Reminder System	Calendar integration for court dates, probation check-ins, and legal deadlines. Multi-channel reminders (SMS, push, email). Supports family members tracking on behalf of incarcerated loved ones.
Policy Advocacy & Petition Tools	Tools for organizing around criminal justice reform: petition creation and signature collection, representative contact lookup, legislative tracking for relevant bills, and campaign coordination features.
User Stories
As a person with a 10-year-old nonviolent conviction, I want to check if I'm eligible for record expungement in my state and get help filing so that I can pass background checks for housing and employment.
As a young person about to attend my first protest, I want to understand my rights in an interactive, easy-to-remember format so that I can protect myself while exercising my First Amendment rights.
As a family member of someone recently released, I want to find reentry resources for housing, employment, and counseling in our area so that my loved one has the support they need to rebuild their life.
As a community organizer, I want to track criminal justice reform bills in my state and mobilize petition signatures so that I can amplify our community's voice in the legislative process.
