Module 6: UPLIFT COMMUNITY — Community Support & Mutual Aid
Tagline: "We are each other's infrastructure. Together, we rise."

Problem Statement
Black communities face disproportionate social isolation, resource fragmentation, disaster vulnerability, and a lack of civic engagement infrastructure. Resources exist — food banks, childcare cooperatives, housing assistance, transportation programs — but they are scattered across dozens of disconnected websites, phone trees, and word-of-mouth networks. When crises hit — from natural disasters to pandemic lockdowns — these fragmented systems collapse. Meanwhile, civic engagement infrastructure (voter registration, town hall access, representative contact) remains difficult to navigate, contributing to the gap between community voice and policy action.

Core Features
Feature	Description
Mutual Aid Request & Fulfillment Board	Community members post needs (groceries, rent assistance, childcare, transportation) and others fulfill them. Reputation system, verification options, and transparent need-fulfillment tracking. Supports monetary and non-monetary assistance.
Community Event Calendar & Organizer Toolkit	Shared calendar of community events: town halls, health fairs, job fairs, cultural celebrations, workshops. Event creation tools with RSVP, promotion, volunteer coordination, and post-event feedback collection.
Volunteer Matching Engine	Connects volunteers with organizations and causes based on skills, availability, interests, and location. Hour tracking for service credits, community recognition, and organizational reporting.
Neighborhood Resource Map	Interactive map aggregating local resources: childcare, transportation, housing assistance, food pantries, legal aid, health clinics, job training, and more. Community-contributed and verified. Filterable, searchable, and available offline.
Crisis & Disaster Response Coordination	Emergency communication tools for natural disasters, community crises, and rapid mutual aid mobilization. Check-in system, resource deployment tracking, and coordination with 211/emergency services.
Civic Engagement Tools	Voter registration and polling place lookup, elected representative contact information, town hall meeting scheduler, ballot measure explainers, and civic education content. Non-partisan voter engagement campaigns.
Community Forum & Storytelling Platform	Moderated discussion forums organized by topic, neighborhood, and interest group. Storytelling feature where community members share experiences, victories, and needs. Content moderation policy co-created with users.
Resource Sharing Marketplace	Sharing economy for the community: tool libraries, skill swaps, time banking, ride shares, and equipment lending. Credit-based system where contributing earns time credits redeemable for other services.
User Stories
As a single mother needing emergency childcare for a job interview, I want to post a mutual aid request and find a vetted community member who can help so that I don't miss a career opportunity.
As a neighborhood leader, I want to create and promote community events with built-in volunteer coordination so that I can organize effectively without juggling five different apps.
As a first-time voter, I want to register to vote, find my polling place, and understand what's on my ballot in plain language so that I can participate meaningfully in elections.
As a community member after a hurricane, I want to check in as safe, see who needs help, and coordinate resource delivery so that our neighborhood recovers faster than waiting for outside aid.
